  "summary": "This refreshing Japanese grain salad delivers a vibrant harmony of chewy pressed barley, crisp cucumbers, shelled edamame, and <b>rich hot-smoked salmon flakes</b>. Infused with a delicate dressing of toasted sesame oil, rice vinegar, and white miso, the salad achieves a balanced contrast between earthy grains and deep smoky notes. The cold grain base absorbs the nutty rice vinegar emulsion thoroughly without losing its satisfying structure, creating a dish that feels hearty yet light on the palate. Brightened with toasted sesame seeds and thinly sliced radishes, every bite provides a delightful crunch paired with savory ocean depth. Perfect as a quick lunch or an elegant side dish for summer entertaining, this grain bowl showcases the refined elegance of Japanese flavor balance. Prepare the barley in advance to allow the grains to fully cool before tossing them with the delicate smoked fish and crisp fresh vegetables.",
